course: dictionary
lesson: 9965
title: One spelling, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word tay is a good example. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «The River Tay is the longest river in Scotland.» The capital letters and the words River and Scotland show that Tay is a name for a place, not a drink.
explain: «a cup of tay» is different. Here tay is an old Irish country way of saying and spelling tea. Swap in tea and the sentence still makes sense, so this tay means the drink.
fact: Tay is a name: the River Tay is the longest river in Scotland, about 190 km long.
fact: The River Tay flows past Perth and into the sea at Dundee.
fact: The Tay Bridge disaster of 1879 happened when a railway bridge fell in a storm.
fact: Tay as a dialect word is an old Irish way of saying and spelling «tea», as in «a cup of tay».
fact: French «le thé» means tea, and it is said "luh TAY", which sounds a lot like tay.
exercise: «The River Tay is the longest river in Scotland.» What kind of word is tay here? | A drink | *A place name | A type of bird | A loud noise
exercise: An Irish granny asks, «Would you like a cup of tay?» What does tay mean? | A big storm | A railway bridge | *A cup of tea | A river in Scotland
exercise: Find the word that tells you tay is a place, not a drink: «The River Tay flows past Perth.» | past | flows | Perth is a town, so it is the sea | *River
test: «The Tay Bridge fell in a storm in 1879.» What happened to the Tay Bridge? | *It fell down in a storm | It flooded the sea | It was painted gold | It was built in a day
test: Which word is the best swap for tay in «a cup of tay»? | Firth | River Tay | Tay Bridge | *tea
exam: Why can you not be sure what tay means from the word alone? | It is a French word only | It is spelled wrong in every dictionary | It has no vowels | *It has two meanings, a river name and an old Irish word for tea, so the context decides
